\ The stack-effect checker: the declaration owner and its arenas, the scan of
\ each definition, and the effect store and records the compiler reads.
\
\ Arenas: owners decide the lifetime. Scratch resets to its boot buffer or
\ takes from the scratch region. No process-local mmap address may enter an
\ image. Growth is geometric, so a store is copied O(log n) times per load.
\
\ The scratch region: per-definition scratch stores take storage from one
\ region that lives as long as the process; their counter, pointer and
\ capacity cells sit in DATA spans that CHECKER-REG:SCRATCH{ and
\ CHECKER-REG:}SCRATCH bracket and mark as scratch, so an image holds them at
\ none, NULL and 0.
\
\ The trail pin: ROWS-PIN marks the trail height at a refusal. Between AT-PIN
\ and ;AT-PIN every store made since the pin is undone, so the tables read as
\ they stood at the pin; ;AT-PIN takes back the view's own compression stores
\ before it restores. An unwind below the pin takes back bindings the pin saw,
\ so the pin falls with it, and AT-PIN still takes back every binding made
\ after the refusal.
\
\ Recursive calls: RECURSE instantiates the effect SIG-EFF-CACHE! built
\ before the body ran, so the kind and restrictions the body later gives a
\ declared quantifier reach no instance. RECUR-CHECK meets each instance with
\ them after the body and pins a failure on the RECURSE that made it.
\
\ The linear discipline: counting concrete linear types on the stack misses a
\ value copied or dropped while its type is still a var that later unifies
\ with a linear type (KEEP's `over`, a quotation's `dup FREE`). Two rules close
\ that gap. LIN-EFF-PASS: a var in an applied effect that binds to a linear
\ type must occur equally on the input and output sides of the whole effect,
\ quotation sub-effects included (KEEP, one in and two out, is refused; DIP
\ and swap pass). A generated constructor, MAKE or UNMAKE row moves exactly
\ its payload, so `LQ2:ERR ( b -- lq2<a,b> )` mints an err without an `a`; an
\ ordinary word with the same effect is still counted. LIN-TAINT and
\ LIN-TAINT-SCAN: a var copied or dropped while polymorphic is tainted, and
\ refused if it later resolves to a linear type (`[: dup FREE ;]`). The
\ discipline runs once a DEFLINEAR type is declared, and also while a type
\ entry may be unread, since a body checked before the read would escape it.
\
\ Rigid identities: a host allocation is stamped by fresh, rigid, never-reused
\ identities that ptr T and type vars cannot express: its REGION (which
\ allocation), EXTENT (bounds) and GENERATION (mutation epoch). Each domain
\ owns a private per-check counter (RGN-N, EXT-N, GEN-N); the atom's domain
\ qualifies the id in ATOM-OK?, so equal ids from different domains never
\ unify. RIGID-MAX bounds every domain below the sign wrap, so a counter
\ throws E-RIGID-EXHAUST before it could wrap and re-grant a live id. Counters
\ reset per check (RIGID-RESET); the bound is settable.
\
\ The compile window: a callback that runs while a definition compiles changes
\ nothing. After the native compiler's scan returns, it opens WRITE-WINDOW with
\ the code a write is refused with, and shuts it with 0 before its own writes
\ and on every exit. Each refusal comes before the first state the pending
\ definition reads moves, so WRITE-WINDOW-CK stands at the only appenders of
\ the checker's stores and type registries, and before any writer that moves a
\ latch or the record symbol first.
\
\ Barrier uniformity: a block collective, a tile-to-uniform reduction or a
\ cp.async wait from committed to ready, lowers to `bar.sync` and deadlocks
\ under divergent predication. E-ADD-EFFECT detects the shape from the
\ recorded din and dout rows (PTX-BARRIER-ROWS?) and flags CTL-BARRIER; the
\ call-site check refuses such a call inside an open control frame.
\
\ Term-walk depth: the recursive term walkers bracket each RECURSE with
\ TWALK-DEEPER and TWALK-SHALLOWER, and each public wrapper resets the depth
\ first. The bound counts depth, not steps, since the native stack is what
\ overflows; a cyclic or mis-indexed term dies with a named diagnostic instead
\ of a SIGSEGV.
\
\ Per-execution identities: `;]`, `[']` (MARK) and a direct call (CALLED) list
\ each rigid identity a quotation mints; each execution pairs those with new
\ identities (START) and renews them in its outputs and callbacks' rows
\ (RENEW). A binding that takes such an identity out of its quotation fails as
\ a mismatch in that identity's domain (HELD); a declared fresh name may take
\ one, which FRESH-CLAIM judges against its signature.
\
\ Hidden layout fields: a layout value of known width W, linear included,
\ stands in a row as W hidden physical field terms (PUSH-LOGICAL), payload
\ slots 0 to W-2 and the tag at W-1 on top. Each reuses the logical family id,
\ name and argument terms and carries its slot plus one in PARAMHID, 0 meaning
\ logical. A hidden term pairs only with the same family and slot and never
\ binds a var, con, ptr or atom. A call expands a logical cell whose width it
\ resolved the same way (OUTPUT-COPY). Whole-bundle transports (dup, swap,
\ >r and kin) move the group by row surgery (XPORT-STEP?). A layout whose
\ width reads an open argument (LAYOUT-WIDTH-OPEN?) stays one logical cell: a
\ transport would bind it to a fresh var, which LAYOUT-XPORT-ALLOW? refuses
\ because an open layout may be linear, and LOC-BIND refuses a locals capture
\ of one; every other touch fails closed. The width and group questions see
\ through a stale wrapper and the type question does not: `catch` stales a
\ window one cell at a time, and a group walker asked on the wrapper would
\ stop seeing the group, leaving W cells no single `drop` removes. A stale
\ cell pairs only with a var or an equally stale cell, so every typed use of
\ the group is still E-STALE-READ.
\
\ Raw cells: a raw storage definer (create, variable, constant) mints a RAW
\ type var, and a fetch from the cell yields that var. RAW-OK? admits a plain
\ scalar, a role con or an atom and raises a var argument to RAW; it refuses a
\ nominal family or layout value, which would forge an arity-0 family
\ identity, a linear con, a pointer and an executable value. Role cons stay
\ admitted because the engine's code generator raw-stores them. Each mention
\ of an undeclared cell re-freshens its scheme's var, so an admitted pointer
\ would launder an integer into an address (`V ! V @ @`); refusing the value
\ at the binding fences every consumer at once. A cell that holds an address
\ or code is declared (PTR-VARIABLE, TYPED-VARIABLE, TYPED-BUFFER,
\ DYNAMIC-BUFFER, `defer`, `xt!`) and its storage word mints the type, so
\ nothing else writes the cell at another type. TVK-ANY vars are unaffected,
\ so a typed fetch, a constructor and role or converter words still bind a
\ family. FENCE-WHY answers for every fenced kind, so the base addresses keep
\ TVK-RAW's admissibility; it meets a var with the kind instead of judging
\ it, which carries the kind through `+`, `cell+`, `1+` and out through `@`.
\
\ Base addresses: neither the null nor the DATA base addresses a declared
\ element, so nothing read through one may be a nominal identity or an
\ address. The null keeps a permissive pointee arm under CUR-STRICT: `ptr
\ thing NULL-PTR =`, the store, the distance and `0=` certify, and only the
\ value position is fenced. The DATA base has no permissive arm: NOMPTR-BLOCK?
\ stops a nominal only at the first pointee, so blocking the pointer term
\ itself closes every depth. The permissive arm still meets, so a wrapper
\ that publishes a derived pointer as `( -- ptr a )` restricts its own
\ quantifier and NP-CHECK refuses it. An executable value is fenced before
\ the null's permissive arm, or `( -- ptr [ -- n ] ) NULL-PTR 8 +` would run
\ at address 8; so a declared code cell cannot be compared with the null, and
\ an empty one is read through a number-typed accessor of the same address.
\ That refusal latches RAW-EXEC-HIT: at every base the repair is to declare
\ the cell that holds the xt.
\
\ Hold frames: while a quotation is compared with a declared callable, the
\ callable's implicit data tail is rigid. The callee runs it on whatever
\ stack it holds and expects the declared rows back, so no row that outlives
\ the comparison may come to equal the tail or hold it. Each comparison
\ pushes a hold frame (HOLD-PUSH): its trail mark, its var floor (a var at or
\ above it was made by the comparison) and K, the unbound implicit tails of
\ the data input and output it holds rigid. The instantiable tails of one
\ UNIFY share one list, which a popped frame leaves in place. By side role, a
\ demanded side's declared tails are rigid; a value's own tails (a literal's
\ or a tick's) are instantiable on either side, since the value runs on any
\ stack; a provided side's declared tails are instantiated on a copy when the
\ other side is demanded, never bound in place, since another value may share
\ the declared var; in a join both sides' declared tails are rigid. A tail
\ already held keeps its role. Return rows are exempt: a quotation literal's
\ return rows are its enclosing definition's. execute and catch instantiate
\ every implicit tail on a copy the same way (QUOT-APPLY-INST) and renew the
\ per-execution identities in its value types; named rows stay shared.
\
\ Logical and hidden layout cells: a stored effect keeps a layout value as one
\ logical cell only when its width reads an open argument. At a boundary, a
\ call site, a join or a loop's back edge that cell can meet the hidden
\ expansion of the same family, W cells wide with a known width. The logical
\ cell expands into hidden fields at its own width (an open argument measures
\ one cell) and the rows pair cell for cell, so a width that disagrees fails
\ the slot pairing; at a join the edge binds the width and both sides join as
\ the W-cell group. A linear payload is counted once, at the group's tag.
\ Transport mode keeps its own group surgery and takes no part.
\
\ Input underflow: the cells below a definition's declared inputs are the
\ caller's. The declared base is an open row, so a step that reaches under it
\ binds it and checking goes on; the boundary check alone would pin the last
\ token, so the token that spends the frame is asked instead. Both depths are
\ read before that step's unify, since afterwards a bound tail makes the two
\ rows one, and the refusal waits for the unify to succeed, so a step both
\ short and mistyped is answered as a mismatch.
\
\ Throw masks: `catch` restores both stacks' depth, never their contents, so a
\ cell of the caught quotation's window (its declared fixed input prefix) keeps
\ its input type only if every throw path of the body left it alone. Each body
\ records one intact mask per stack: bit j, counted from the top of the window,
\ is set while every edge so far left window cell j alone. Bits count from the
\ top because the window grows downward as the body pops and is final only at
\ `;]`: a cell popped after an edge lay below that edge's stack pointer and is
\ intact there, and top-relative bits keep naming the same cell as the window
\ deepens. Bits above the recorded width mean intact too, so a window wider
\ than the mask, or a row an edge cannot be compared against, records zero. A
\ cell is intact only when the edge holds the same term, not one that unifies
\ with it: a quotation literal's window cells are unbound until the catch site
\ fits them, and binding one would choose a type for the caller.
\
\ Engine-word identity: a rule that types an engine word by what it does may
\ judge a token only when the token binds that word, since `@` in a package
\ that defines `@`, or `dup` after `undefine dup`, is another word of the same
\ spelling. The identity is kept apart from the effect, registered where the
\ engine defines the word, and travels with the control flags in two forms:
\ CTL-CORE-OP marks the engine's own word of a spelling within a family a rule
\ chooses by spelling, and CTL-INTRINSIC holds a five-bit id naming one engine
\ word, for the rules that dispatch on the word itself. `undefine` retires
\ both, a redefinition records none, and an export does not copy them.
\
\ Unjudged scans: a TRUSTED: body's scan is the width authority tier 0 lowers
\ from whatever its verdict, so a rejected token there still leaves the rows
\ its runtime leaves. DO-TOK1 arms UNJ-TOK for each unjudged token. A failed
\ committed step (never inside a TRY-EFF trial), or a failed token no step
\ settled, applies its declared effect to the pre-token rows: pop exactly the
\ input's physical cells and push the declared outputs over the remainder. A
\ failure that cannot be spliced while a row holds a wide or open-width cell
\ sets SCAN-INCOMPLETE, and so does a lost local bind with a local declared
\ wide (LOC-UNJ-BIND); the certificate then says NEEDS-INCOMPLETE. Otherwise
\ the unspliced result stands and every cell lowers at the default width. A
\ spliced call whose unify never reached the row tail freezes its declared
\ rows there, so its call record states the cells the splice popped and
\ pushed; CHECK finalizes an unjudged scan's call records whatever its
\ verdict.
\
\ The return row: >r, r> and r@ move types between DCUR and RCUR, and a
\ definition must leave the return row exactly as it found it (ANS 3.2.3.3).
\ The row's base is the definition's SGRBASE (SGRIN, the row its `|` clause
\ carries, else RBROW), or inside a quotation literal the literal's own RBROW.
\ A read short of cells does not fail where it reads: the base is an open row,
\ so the unify binds it. So a read measures the row before the unify, as
\ STEP-BORROWS? measures the data row, and is refused at its own token once
\ the unify has fit (RS-BORROWS?). The final balance check rejects net growth,
\ and a return base bound with no read (CHECK-NO-BORROW, QUOT-RSEAL); loop
\ joins unify RCUR too.
\
\ What a catch site hands back: the fit check proves the caught body takes and
\ leaves the same stack, not that the throw paths leave the cells they were
\ given. Each window cell the folded mask does not vouch for becomes
\ `stale<t>` on the live row; the throw code `catch` pushes is a plain `n`
\ added after. Mask bits count from the top, so the rewrite walks down to the
\ window's bottom and rebuilds the entries above it: the entry at depth d
\ takes bit d, and a depth past the mask's reach was never vouched for. The
\ walk ends at the counted window or a non-push term (the row's tail); it is
\ as deep as the window is wide, so it needs no scratch row and declines no
\ width.
\
\ The signature parser: a single lowercase letter is a type variable shared
\ across in/out of one signature; `n` = int (con 1), `f` = flag (CC-BOOL); an
\ unknown multi-char token marks the signature malformed. Row variables are
\ shared, so the effect is row-polymorphic. Quantifiers keep their source
\ letter; this is not the declaration parameter alphabet. Facts text names a
\ variable past the letters by its ordinal.
\
\ The refusal a definition's diagnostic names: one failure refuses a
\ definition, and every diagnostic field describes that one, chosen by load
\ order. The body compiles before `;` checks anything, so the first body token
\ the load cannot compile (undefined word, retired global, unbindable local,
\ unmodeled immediate, unreadable construct or match) refuses it (CREFUSE,
\ taken by REFUSAL-STEP). A name `using` makes the walk refuse
\ (CHECKER-RESOLVE:RAISE) is such a token when ticked or when no global binds
\ it. Otherwise, in order: the first name a used public shadows a global for
\ or makes ambiguous beside one (CUSING); a signature that does not parse
\ (SGBAD-FAIL!); the first token whose check fails (REFUSAL-OF); the checks at
\ `;` (REFUSAL@).
\
\ Stored type spans: a storage declaration's stored type is read token by
\ token at run time and at the gate. The spelling ends at the first token
\ other than a `ptr` prefix that leaves no bracket open, counting the `<` `[`
\ `>` `]` NEXT-SIG-TOK splits out, so a pointer chain, family application and
\ spaced quotation or scheme reach SIG-TYPE whole; a stray closer ends it and
\ SIG-TYPE refuses it. The declaration also ends with its line: the name
\ stands on the definer's line and the type's first token on the name's. A
\ line feed between tokens, as no next token does, leaves the token to the
\ next statement: a missing name or type is refused by name
\ (CHECKER-STORAGE-NAME-REFUSE, CHECKER-STORAGE-TYPE-REFUSE) and SIG-TYPE
\ refuses a span left open.
\
\ Callable contracts: a stored callable must implement every instantiation its
\ declared quotation admits. QCON-BEGIN saves the contract's type and row
\ variables before ordinary unification; QCON-OK? then checks that fitting the
\ implementation did not specialize, narrow, or merge them, nor restrict a type
\ variable to a cast's stored types (NLINEAR). Both `is` and a typed quotation
\ cell use this same contract rule.
\
\ Declaration locations: the armed location (CHECKER-DECL-AT!) is the declaring
\ token of the statement being registered: its name, borrowed from the arming
\ caller, its file visit and its byte range. A named registrar attaches it to
\ the record it retained (DL-TAKE), copying the name; DL-NEW is that record when
\ the registrar's own step built one, and the registrar zeroes it before a step
\ that may retain nothing. DECL-LOCS holds one row per located record,
\ ascending by offset, its names appended in row order to their own bytes; a
\ use copies a row out when it binds (NAV-USE). The tables are process-local:
\ no record field, wire format, unit file or image carries them.
\
\ The symbol hash index: a process-local mmap cache; SYMS and the
\ USIGS/NORETS/DFERS/PES stores stay authoritative. Buckets map folded
\ (pkg,vis,name) to a symbol id and mirror SYMS exactly: SYM-INTERN pushes new
\ rows front, scope exit retires rows newest-first (each retired row is at its
\ bucket head), anything else rebuilds from SYMS. The table is sized and masked
\ by SYM-CAP and is rehashed at a new cap on the next lookup. Per-symbol cells
\ memoize the current effect record offset, control flags, defer flag and first
\ prim slot, valid only while their epoch cell equals HIDX-EPOCH; the sync
\ words catch every store rewind or swap (UEND/USIGS-P, NORET-END) and bump the
\ epoch, invalidating the whole cache at once. Snapshot prepare drops the
\ mapping; a restored image rebuilds lazily.
\
\ The interpret row: CHECKER-TOP-SAVE and CHECKER-TOP-LOAD copy it with the
\ same node copier as stored effects, but into two process-owned buffers instead
\ of USIGS, while TOP-COPYING is set. A save writes the write buffer from terms
\ whose atom and family names still borrow the read buffer, then the two swap.
\ A literal event appends to the read buffer at TOP-READ-END.
\
\ Node interning: when E-COPY* finishes a subterm at the top of the arena, an
\ identical node below wins: UEND rewinds over the fresh copy and the older
\ offset is answered. The hash only chooses a chain; every hit compares the
\ nodes, since a hash collision would certify a word against another word's
\ signature. Children are interned before their parent, so equal tags and key
\ cells at the roots mean equal subterms; only an atom's or param's name bytes,
\ written per copy, are compared by content. E-KEY-N and E-KEY are the one
\ description of a node's identity, read by both hash and compare. Var ids are
\ the stored ones: E-COPY* renumbers vars in first-appearance order, and
\ E-TV-ID/E-RV-ID still run for a subterm interned away, since it is built
\ before it is discarded. The rewind is safe: a finished subterm spans its root
\ to UEND and names only offsets below that top, so no surviving node names a
\ byte above a truncation point. A forgotten intern (rewind, snapshot) costs
\ hits, never correctness.
\
\ The intern index is made exact before each lookup (UIX-EXACT). With no table,
\ in a fresh process or after a snapshot boot, it is allocated and built from
\ the store, which may already be full. After a rewind this file did not
\ perform (UEND below the mark), or under a base no relocation carried the
\ stamp to (a fresh mapping, an arena swapped in), the entries are forgotten
\ and rebuilt from the current store. Otherwise the store only grew and the new
\ end is marked. A verbatim relocation is no move: USIGS-GROW carries the stamp.
\ The rebuild walks the store's records, and the store's layout is the visited
\ set: a record owns the bytes up to the next record, exactly the nodes, name
\ bytes and arg runs E-COPY wrote for its rows (a discarded node was rewound
\ before the next append), so each span is reachable from its record's four row
\ roots and a child outside it is an older record's, already visited. Each span
\ is walked once with a range test per older reference; a record that appended
\ nothing is skipped whole. The table's lookup still gates the span, since a
\ record may name one of its nodes twice.
\
\ The per-symbol effect-record index (USX): a symbol lookup needs one record,
\ the newest carrying that symbol; older ones are shadowed and its state
\ (active or deleted) is the answer. HT-USX keeps its offset+1 per symbol id.
\ It is exact, not a memo, kept by three seams. On append, E-REC-START links the
\ new record (ER.SYMPREV = old head) and makes it the head. On truncation,
\ USIGS-RESTORE-END walks only the discarded records and resets each affected
\ head to the surviving record below. An arena swap, a foreign rewind or a
\ symbol-table grow is detected structurally (non-monotone UEND, changed store
\ identity, dropped mapping) and the index is rebuilt. The append seam syncs
\ before it writes, so regrowth over truncated offsets cannot mask a rewind.
\
\ Source-order visibility under the binding horizon: a replay checks a
\ definition as the engine compiles it and sees exactly the records that existed
\ then. A reconstruction checks recorded source in an engine already holding it
\ and everything after, so a token would bind the newest record of its
\ spelling, maybe a later shadow (a package word declared after a definition
\ that named its global twin). Inside a verifier scope CHECK latches the
\ definition's own record as BIND-HORIZON and lookups see only records before
\ it. Outside one (the live load path, a candidate probe whose name is a label)
\ the whole store is seen, and so is it for a definition the store does not
\ know. Nothing is hidden by name or for being older, so a package dependency
\ still binds. Always visible: what the pass itself recorded (PASS-FLOOR), since
\ the text verified may differ from the text on record and a word it defined
\ earlier is what a cold compile would see; and a seeded record, whose offset
\ says when the pool was first missed on its name, not when the word was
\ defined (boot).
\
\ Navigation, what a use bound: a use is reported at the five places one source
\ occurrence resolves: a body token (BIND-TOK), a swallowed `[']` or `is` target
\ (IS-TARGET-SYM), a top-level token or tick (TOP-ANSWER), an export operand
\ (EXPORT-RESOLVE) and a `generates:` definer (CHECKER-GENERATES), never from
\ CHECKER-BIND itself. It takes the location of the record the binding selects
\ at that moment, the newest one under BIND-HORIZON, never an older row's, and
\ 0 0 0 when that record has none: a word the image holds has none. A primitive
\ has no record, but its binding still reports its symbol. A tombstone reports
\ nothing. The use is the spelling's byte range in its source (NAV-SRC-XT); a
\ spelling the source map does not hold reports nothing.
\
\ The completion cursor: the verifier arms a cursor's offset in the next text
\ it checks, with the visitor its candidates go to (CHECKER-CURSOR!). The check
\ that takes the arm (CUR-TAKE) owns it for its whole run, retries included: an
\ attempt that reaches the cursor keeps the spellings that bind there in the
\ pending table, a retry drops its attempt's rows, and at its exit the owner
\ publishes the final attempt's with its uses and disarms (PUBLISH-EXIT). A
\ visitor gets a spelling, borrowed for the call, and the file visit and
\ half-open byte range of the declaration row that gave it, or 0 0 0 when no
\ row locates it. One arm at a time: arming over an arm, and arming, disarming
\ or enumerating while a check owns one or a visitor runs, throws
\ E-CURSOR-NESTED before it touches either.
\
\ Created effects: DOESEFF carries the effect a `create … does>` definer gives
\ its created words from the clause check, which sees the clause but not the
\ definer's name, to the definer's body check, which sees the name but not the
\ clause. The native compiler checks the definer first and sets the latch at
\ its publication. The latch (DOESPEND) fails closed, since the two checks also
\ run in the other order and a latch left armed would teach the next record
\ that an ordinary word creates something. Every body check steps it: a
\ certified clause becomes a body check under way, and any other state clears.
\ Only that body check's record takes it (DOES-EFF-TAKE); a refused clause
\ clears instead of arming, and a publication clears what it left. The
\ unjudged scan is no body check: on return it restores the latch, a TRUSTED:
\ definer's publication steps it, and on a throw it clears. A wrapper of a
\ definer inherits the same effect when its body makes exactly one definer call
\ on a straight line, with no control frame, quotation, `exit`, `leave` or
\ `recurse`: the walk of every certified body counts the calls (WRAPN, WRAPC)
\ and notes any bend (WRAPBENT), since a wrapper compiled in this process has
\ no text. Every walk that is not a definition's own body clears these, and a
\ candidate never inherits: its record is truncated when the scope ends.
\
\ The checker overlay: a replay binds every name through the engine's own
\ lookup, so while it runs the engine's dictionary holds what a compile of the
\ replayed text would have defined, kept through the replay writers only
\ CHECKER-OVERLAY may call. replay-open saves NDICT, CP, WIDN, CURRENT, the
\ package cells and the using band; on every exit, clean or thrown, the log is
\ undone newest first and replay-close zeroes the overlay's records and restores
\ them; while a task is live it retires those records instead and keeps NDICT
\ and CP, restoring the rest. The outermost asking scope opens the overlay: the
\ verifier window (tag -1) or a package-neutral rollback scope (its frame
\ depth). A scope opened inside it saves the engine scope in a snapshot row and
\ restores it on close, so names a scope publishes bind until the overlay
\ closes. Between a logged record's restore and the drop of a replay record of
\ the same name, one wordlist holds two live records of it: CLOSE ends that
\ window with replay-close and ROLLBACK with ndict!, each before any lookup.
\ Every writer refusal ends the process, so each refusal a replay can meet is
\ checked in CHECKER-OVERLAY first and thrown by name.
\
\ Replayed package scope: live compilation splits each package and using word
\ between the engine and the checker. The engine's keyword moves its scope and
\ notifies the checker, which records the name. A replay reads source as text
\ and compiles nothing, so inside the verifier window the checker overlay moves
\ the engine's scope first. CHECKER-USING-PUSH and CHECKER-USING-POP serve the
\ replay alone: outside the window they refuse rather than move a scope no
\ compile is in.
\
\ Storage declaration refusals: a storage definer refuses a declaration whose
\ type it cannot size, that has no name or one it cannot publish, or whose
\ count is a literal outside its extent or a token the gate cannot certify.
\ The gate pre-pass and the run-time definers both refuse through
\ CHECKER-STORAGE-REFUSE, which reports the declared word and the refused
\ token. Like TRUST-STALE it is a hard stop on the ordinary load path, and is
\ rendered and counted under a MULTI-ERROR load; either way nothing is
\ registered or defined. The diagnostic carries a file position only while the
\ verifier window replays recorded source, for a token inside the buffer that
\ pass registered (CHECKER-VERIFY-SOURCE!, STGR-IN-SOURCE?). A run-time
\ definer reads its tokens from the input, whose place in its file the checker
\ has no record of.
\
\ Name binding: one lookup binds a name, and it is the engine's. `scope-find`
\ runs what the compiler's call site runs, so the checker certifies the record
\ the compiler calls; the checker only answers which of its symbols that record
\ is (the wordlist names the scope, the tail names the row). A record with no
\ checker symbol is not certifiable: 0, and E-UNDEFINED at the call site. A
\ token binds the record the lookup binds, a definition recorded and not yet
\ published (CK-PENDING-SYM), or a keyword's axiom (CK-AXIOM-SYM). Other
\ symbols with no engine record (a TRUST with no body, a name only the source
\ pre-verifier registered) bind nowhere, bare or qualified. An owner-private
\ primitive row binds only as the owner's view of the engine's global record,
\ which the engine holds once (CK-REC-BIND). The engine finds a bare name in
\ the open package whatever current is, so the binding asks PKG-LIVE-XT for
\ the open package.
\
\ The pending window: the store is one definition ahead of the dictionary. A
\ definition is recorded when its check certifies it or TRUST-DECL registers
\ it, and published only after compiling, yet both compilers ask about it by
\ name in between. So the definition recorded last answers a token whose
\ record path in the current scope is its symbol, ahead of the lookup. The
\ stores state the window, not a flag: `ndict@` has not moved since the
\ record, and the record is still its symbol's newest (CK-PEND-SYM). Only a
\ check run while the engine holds the definition unpublished opens it
\ (CK-LIVE-PEND?, CK-CLOSE!); a publication, a truncation, a rollback and
\ `undefine` each end it. A recovery record opens no window: under a hook the
\ native compiler abandons its definition and leaves `ndict@`, so the window
\ would outlive it. A replay compiles nothing, so it opens no window either:
\ inside the verifier window the checker overlay makes the engine's dictionary
\ answer for text it has not compiled, and every exit closes the overlay.
\
\ Candidate scopes: a candidate scope (CHECKER-CANDIDATE-SCOPE-START) checks
\ definitions published together after it closes or not at all, and a row may
\ call an earlier one (a product's derived HASH calls its UNMAKE). While one
\ is open, a symbol whose newest record lies past the outermost scope's floor,
\ with nothing published since, is pending (CK-SCOPE-PENDING?). A scope's
\ close rewinds its records, so a row pends only in its scope and those nested
\ in it. Nothing inside a candidate scope writes the live window.
\
\ The lookup under a binding horizon: in a reconstruction the engine's lookup
\ can return a record of a word defined after the definition being checked, a
\ later package twin, used public or global. HORIZON-FIND hides that record
\ for the time of the lookup and asks again, until every record it reports is
\ visible, so the token binds what a compile at that point bound; `finally`
\ gives the hidden records back on every exit. A record lies beyond the
\ horizon when every record of its symbol does (SYM-BEYOND?); one the store
\ never recorded is the engine's own word and stays. NAME-TOK sets a horizon
\ only inside the verifier window, so the overlay is open whenever one is set.
\
\ The binder's answers: LIVE-BIND answers its refusals rather than raising
\ them. It leaves ( sym why ), why 0 or the code of the refusal it reached:
\ CHECKER-REJECT-RC when no authority names a package context for a bare
\ token, E-USING-SHADOW-GLOBAL when a used public also exports the tail a
\ global binds, E-USING-AMBIGUOUS when two used publics export it and nothing
\ earlier binds it or the global does. Under a refusal sym is no answer. It
\ renders nothing: a using refusal leaves the used packages holding the tail
\ marked in CK-USED-MASK for the raise to name. CHECKER-BIND raises the
\ refusal (CHECKER-RESOLVE:RAISE); a caller that only asks reads why. A name
\ the split refuses (a malformed qualified name, or a length that describes no
\ memory) binds nothing. A sym of 0 without a refusal does not prove the load
\ cannot bind the name, since the engine holds words no checker symbol names
\ (one defined undeclared under `0 set-check`); LIVE-BIND sets WALK-REC when
\ its answer is the record the engine's lookup found.
\
\ Native multi-error recovery: under a hook the native compiler abandons a
\ refused definition instead of publishing it, so in a multi-error run the
\ engine's lookup cannot see the recovery row (RECOVERY-ROW?) of a word a
\ later definition calls; on x86-64 every definition is native. A recovery row
\ is sound only while a body is checked or compiled: the native compiler
\ withholds publication of any body that used one. In the compile window the
\ compiler asks only about the definition and the words its body names; a
\ body name binds what the walk bound, so its use already withheld the
\ definition. The definition's own name binds its own recovery row, which
\ opens no pending window. A top-level step runs what it binds, and EXPORT
\ publishes it, at once. So only under MULTI-ERR? inside a body's walk
\ (BODY-WALK) or the compile window does a recovery row bind ahead of the
\ lookup's record (RECOVERY-BIND), in the engine's search order: the open
\ package's private then public wordlist, inside a part its package's private
\ then public one, the globals, then the used publics in import order. A
\ qualified name asks its package's public row, and the global row when that
\ package is open. A hookless compile finds a refused definition by this bind.
\
\ Rendering marks: a top-level statement that calls a CTL-RENDERS word defines
\ words, and may register nominal types, from text the source pre-pass never
\ reads. The pre-pass marks the wordlist current then with a symbol whose name
\ holds a space, which no token can spell; the mark carries no effect and
\ retires with its scope's symbols. A body token that resolves nowhere defers
\ its definition to the run only when its lookup walks a marked wordlist, and
\ an unresolved nominal type defers when its resolution reaches a type mark.
\ A direct type registrar marks its own declaration section; rendered source
\ can open any package, so its type mark is global. The limit: a word the
\ checker already holds resolves first, so a definition shadowing it is judged
\ against it; deferring every name behind a mark would defer every global a
\ marked section calls.
\
\ Instantiated layout widths: a parametric family instantiated with a
\ multi-cell argument occupies more cells than its declaration reserves
\ (`option<obj:line>` needs two payload cells), and the instantiated width is a
\ function of a resolved type term. So the checker records it per token in the
\ call-fact table under its own kind, which the definition reset, the retry
\ cursor and capture cleanup cover. A MATCH family token records its
\ instantiated bundle width, an arm's `of` token its instantiated pad count, and
\ a construction's token the cells its instantiation adds beyond the declared
\ width: a difference, since the construction's lowering already pushes the
\ declared pads. These are width facts, not lowering-certificate rows. Dispatch
\ requires a fact; a construction needs none unless its instantiation adds
\ cells.
\
\ Shadowed arity: while a package is open, the engine and the checker resolve
\ a bare tail private-first, so a public definition whose bare tail a private
\ word of the same package claims does not bind its own name, and the native
\ compiler would elaborate the public word against the private word's arity.
\ The pair stays legal; E-SHADOWED-ARITY refuses only two declared effects that
\ move different numbers of cells, at the second definition, and only for a
\ colon definition with a declared signature. A pair whose widths cannot be
\ judged is left to the native compiler's own arity refusal.
\
\ Buffer counts: a buffer definer's count is the token before the definer,
\ read and never run, since no static pass models the interpret stack. An
\ integer token is the count, held to the definer's extent bound; no token is
\ no count. A count named by a word certifies by that word's effect, and a
\ refused or undefined name refuses. A word that takes input ends an
\ expression the line computes, which the definer bounds at load. A word that
\ takes none must hand a `( n -- )` consumer its value: return stack untouched
\ and an output row that unifies with its input row plus one `n`. So a
\ `constant`, an engine-held constant and a colon `( -- n )` qualify, and a
\ `variable` and a `bool` do not. The definer bounds the value at load, so a
\ constant of 0 certifies here and fails there. The unification binds only in
\ per-definition scratch that NEW clears.
\
\ Width facts: per checked definition the checker records one row for every
\ operation whose lowering needs a logical layout width, keyed by the
\ operation's raw source-byte offset and an operand position. Transport and
\ locals rows use logical operand positions; layout-memory rows use position 0
\ for the operation's bundle width, the address itself staying one cell. An
\ absent row means scalar lowering. Certificate consumers query the table
\ before emitting the operation. The table is per-check scratch.
\
\ Storable layouts: `!` and `@` through a `ptr family<..>` address move the
\ pointee's whole logical value, and the address type picks the arm: a bare
\ `ptr a` store of a layout value stays refused, a mismatched family fails
\ ordinary unification, an `n` cannot enter an enum slot, and a fetched value
\ is born typed. Every closed non-linear layout width is admitted, and its
\ registry width is recorded as a width fact before the step changes the row.
\ The effect rows push the family's hidden expansion, so the value side pairs
\ hidden to hidden. A nominal-scalar pointee (an arity-0 cell parameter) takes
\ the same arm with parameter-to-parameter rows but records no width fact:
\ every raw cell is a valid value of the family, so it lowers as a scalar.
\
\ Layout transport: a layout value is W consecutive hidden cells, tag on top
\ and slot 0 deepest. A stack op (`swap`, `rot`, `>r` and the rest) whose top
\ k logical operands include such a group cannot use the primitive's
\ variable-based effect, since a hidden field never binds a variable, so the
\ checker reads k logical groups off the row and pushes them back in the op's
\ output order. A hidden tag opens a group of exactly W cells, checked from
\ slot W-1 down to 0 as one family; a malformed group dies 76. Any other cell
\ is a one-cell group, and a row variable yields a fresh one-cell variable
\ group. A read below the declared inputs, or below the return cells the
\ definition pushed, is an underflow measured as a plain step measures it. An
\ operand carrying a proof or lost metadata takes this path too, scalars
\ included. An operand that is a layout cell of open width sends the whole op
\ to the one-cell path, which refuses it: an open width reads a payload
\ variable that may bind linear. A group moves whole, and the op's linear
\ count is taken before and checked after: a move keeps it, while a copy
\ raises it and a drop lowers it, both refused. A hidden group's linear
\ payload counts once, at its tag. A one-cell variable group the op copies or
\ drops may launder a linear value, so it is tainted. An argument still open
\ in an expanded group is one the width does not read: it occurs only under a
\ pointer, a quotation or an unread slot, owns no payload, and has nothing to
\ launder. A linear group captured into a local leaves the counted rows, so
\ the same check refuses the bind.
\
\ Locals: `{: a b :}` pops and binds names to type variables, and a reference
\ pushes its binding; a later group binds only its own names. A local is known
\ by its declared spelling: a reference must match the declaration's raw bytes
\ byte for byte, while word lookup stays case-insensitive, so a body that
\ declares `text` and writes `TEXT` names the word TEXT. The token reader hands
\ the locals words the raw token beside the folded one; folding changes no
\ byte count and moves no `:`, so one colon position serves both.
\
\ Unjudged local binds: a local bind refused in an unjudged scan still binds at
\ run time, so each local takes the cells the run binds into it. A declared
\ local takes its type's cells, and a layout its full group, though the local
\ holds the group's one-cell tag term; an undeclared local takes the cell group
\ it lies over in the row before the token, one cell or a whole hidden group,
\ read as a transport reads a group. That row is read from the top local down,
\ before the bind unifies anything, and reads no width for a declared layout
\ of open width, or for an undeclared local over a logical layout cell, part
\ of a hidden group, or the row's open tail. A later reference then pushes the
\ cells the run bound, and the lowering binds the widths recorded here. The
\ token's width facts state the declared groups instead, and the second
\ compile pass checks them against those widths. One splice pops the declared
\ row's cells off the rows before the token. A bind with an unknown width is
\ lost, since what the run bound is unknown, and leaves the scan incomplete
\ where a width is at stake: a wide cell in the rows before the token, or a
\ local declared wide, hidden or of open width, which binds more cells than
\ the row shows. An undeclared local is one cell unless those rows hold a wide
\ one.
\
\ MATCH: `MATCH family variant OF ... ENDOF ... ;MATCH` is a checker control
\ form. The family and variant tokens are captured before locals, control and
\ word dispatch. OF and ENDOF are shared with CASE and told apart by the
\ control frame's kind: 9 is a match and 10 a match branch, where CASE is 7
\ and 8. MATCH pops the scrutinee's hidden-field bundle, slot 0 through the
\ tag, checking each cell against the resolved family, and recovers the
\ family's type arguments from the tag term. Each branch checks from the base
\ row plus that variant's instantiated payload. Branch outputs unify at ENDOF.
\ ;MATCH checks that every variant has a branch, against a tag bitset in
\ declaration order since there is no default branch, and installs the joined
\ rows. Match frames live in a growable side arena with a growable pool of
\ seen bitsets. Every structural failure latches MREJ, a hard reject ranked
\ above uncheckable. Only a width-expanded bundle matches, linear included; a
\ layout whose width reads an open argument is one logical cell with no
\ payload cells, and is refused.
\
\ String payloads: the reader spends a string literal's payload without
\ tokenising it and reports the bytes to the stage that compiles the literal.
\ The span is raw, while an escaped body is what its escapes decode to and is
\ shorter than its text, so span and bytes are recorded apart. A payload was
\ spent exactly when SKF, the skip's close flag, is set: only the two loops
\ that walk a payload to its closing quote set it, so neither the token's
\ spelling nor the verdict decides (the reader may never reach the payload of
\ a name token, a match arm or a token in a locals group). A recorded span was
\ consumed and its escapes validated; an invalid escape spends the rest of the
\ payload and leaves SKF clear.
\
\ Source map: a refusal packet names where its token lies in the checked file.
\ A driver that checks text it copied out of a file arms DIAG-SOURCE! with the
\ scanned bytes and the file line, column and byte of their first byte, and
\ before each check hands DIAG-MAP! the text it built with a table of the runs
\ it copied: one two-cell row per run (text offset, source offset), ascending
\ from text offset 0. DIAG-LOCATE maps a pointer into that text, or into the
\ source, to a file position. The engine arms the map for a definition it
\ captured from a file buffer, from the rows the capture records, and gives a
\ body its closer. Text with no map keeps the DIAG-ORIGIN! rule: `evaluate`
\ text other than a slice of the file being loaded, stdin and a program file
\ read without `--load`, a definition whose name lies outside the buffer being
\ read, and the definitions the checker generates for a declaration.
\ DIAG-CLOSER! takes the source token that closes the mapped definition (its
\ `;` or a definer's `does>`), which the text does not hold: a control
\ structure still open there is refused at that token, as the load's compiler
\ refuses it.
\
\ Completion: CHECKER-RESOLVE:EACH-VISIBLE visits, once each, every folded
\ spelling that starts with a prefix and that a position's own selection binds:
\ a body token's walk (VISIBLE-BODY), a top-level token's (VISIBLE-TOP), or a
\ body's named operand, a tick or `is` target no local answers
\ (VISIBLE-NAMED). A word comes with its selected record's DECL-LOCS row
\ (visit, start, end; 0 0 0 for none), a local with 0 0 0. A spelling is taken
\ only when its walk answers why = 0 and binds a symbol or, under live
\ authority, the record the engine's lookup found. Every walk output is put
\ back after the walk, so the token at the cursor binds as it would unasked;
\ nothing is interned or kept. Candidates are every dictionary record's and
\ every live symbol's name. A prefix PKG:tail asks each behind its PKG. Any
\ other prefix asks each bare, behind the open package's name (the engine's
\ top-level find takes PKG:TAIL for a global TAIL while PKG is open), and each
\ public symbol and public-wordlist record behind its package. The whole
\ spelling is compared with the whole prefix, so L, LSP and LSP: each reach
\ LSP:MAIN. The selection decides, not the source.
\
\ Captured effect graphs: a graph a seed carries is checked in three passes
\ before it is imported. The structural pass proves a finite acyclic graph of
\ well-formed nodes. The relevance pass records, per node, a mask of the binders
\ outside it that its descendants can name; a forall body consumes bit zero and
\ shifts its other references toward the new caller. The lexical pass checks how
\ each reference is reached: input position, scheme placement, a family's scope
\ slot, and whether storage has cut off scope access. A child shared at two
\ depths is revisited at the shallower depth, where a free bound variable is
\ visible. A memo hit needs matching domains for the outer binders the node can
\ name, so paths differing only in unused domains share one result.
\
\ The cast walk: CAST-INTRO? and CAST-MAY-LINEAR? walk a cast's terms through
\ pointees, quotation rows and layout members. A layout's members can name the
\ layout again (an ENUM variant may hold a pointer to its own family), so the
\ walk keeps the path of layouts it is expanding, outermost first, each with the
\ sign it was reached at, and expands an instance once per path: the same family
\ over the same argument terms, reached at the same sign, has the same members
\ and gives the same answer. A member is instantiated over its owner's own
\ argument terms, so a recursive member names the same terms, not copies; past
\ CAST-PATH-CAP nested layouts the walk dies rather than guess. An expansion
\ pops what it pushed; CAST-WALK-RESET empties the path after a throw.
\ CAST-MAY-LINEAR? counts a type variable without NLINEAR, as TV! checks each
\ binding of one with it, and walks pointees, quotation rows and layout
\ members, since a projection hands out what they reach; cell-family arguments
\ are phantom, and a scope or region variable binds no value. A quotation whose
\ in and out rows end in one tail passes that tail through; one whose tails
\ differ hands out values it never took.
\
\ Rollback frames: every checker scope and candidate probe pushes a frame
\ holding every mutable high-water mark, and its end pops it, so nested
\ candidates and scopes cannot overwrite a parent's marks. Registries loaded
\ after the checker keep parallel marks through the REG-EXT-RB words, in
\ lockstep since every push pairs with one pop.
\
\ Seeded words: a body naming a seeded word whose row is not yet taken queues
\ the name, and its pass judges the name unbound. CHECK-RETRY runs the pass,
\ takes the names it could not resolve, and runs the pass again. Every pass
\ either creates an effect for a (package, visibility, name) the checker did
\ not have, of which the pool holds finitely many, or creates none and is the
\ last, so the loop ends. It wraps CHECK, not CHECK!, so the source tape's
\ verdict and the certificate producer see the definition's answer once. A
\ candidate and a prefix read run the same loop, since a bare CHECK cannot see
\ a seeded word whose row was never taken in this process; rows a retry takes
\ inside a candidate's rollback frame are popped with it and re-taken at the
\ next miss.
\
\ Refusing a definition: a refusal of the definition (REFUSE-DEF) leaves the
\ walk by a throw, from a body, a does> clause or a top-level token alike.
\ DEF-REFUSED rethrows any other code. On the ordinary load path the refusal
\ stops the load and DEF-STOPPED keeps its code. In a multi-error load it
\ refuses the definition as a rejected verdict does: the walk and its retries
\ end at the refusal, what the walk left set is cleared, the record step runs
\ as CHECK runs it for a refusal, and the load goes on to the next definition.
\ The packet is the definition's diagnostic; nothing else renders.
\
\ The interpret row: a segment is a saved row and the row's two buffers, keyed
\ by the evaluator stack base (a closed `evaluate` reads a different floor) and
\ the evaluate levels ENTRY..LEVEL it spans (the engine's EVALD). Text a running
\ word evaluates on the same base fires one level deeper, before the word's
\ outputs exist, so it gets its own segment: the word's step already saved
\ them. A top-level `evaluate` step widens its segment one level
\ (TOP-WORD-STEP), so the text it reads continues the row. The live segment
\ sits in TOP-READ-P / TOP-WRITE-P and their kin; the enclosing segments are
\ parked in TOP-SEG rows, newest last. EVALD is process-wide, so an event at
\ level lvl means no evaluate frame deeper than lvl is linked: a segment that
\ entered deeper is dead and is released (TOP-SEG-PRUNE). A fresh segment
\ enters at the event's level, which no surviving segment exceeds, so the
\ parked rows and the live one are ordered by ENTRY and the dead ones are
\ always on top. An event selects the segment spanning its stack base at its
\ evaluate level, once the dead ones are gone: the live one, a parked one
\ (dropping the segments above it), or a fresh empty one parked over the live
\ one (CHECKER-TOP-SEGMENT).
\
\ Seeded words at top level: a seeded engine's rows come in at first
\ reference (CK-AOT-INTAKE), and a body takes them between its passes
\ (CHECK-RETRY). The interpret row takes them between passes of one step
\ (TOP-STEP-RETRY): a step over a name the checker does not bind queues it
\ (CALL-UNDEFINED, TOP-TICK-STEP). A tick step is admitted checked with an
\ opaque xt. A word step is held while a seeded row answers the name
\ (TOP-JUDGE), admitted when a rendering statement in scope may define it, and
\ refused otherwise. When a seeded row answers the queue, the step's terms are
\ released, the row taken and the step run again over a fresh load. The saved
\ row the step loads from is not written between passes, so a pass costs the
\ step alone. Each pass takes a row the tables lacked, so the loop ends as a
\ body's does.
\
\ A capture keeps every checker symbol the engine holds.
package CHECKER-REG
\ DECL-CELL is the record the engine certifies through; TARGET-DECL-CELL is the
\ image's own record: inside a build a store to it reaches the image being
\ written, never the builder's checker.
